## 🏗️ Builder Layout Refactoring Prompt

---

### Context

The Arkan builder workspace is composed of the following layout components located in `src/modules/ai-content/adapters/components/builder/layout/`:

- **`BuilderWorkspace.tsx`** — Root orchestrator. Manages fullscreen, onboarding, zoom, and composes all layout pieces.
- **`BuilderLayout.tsx`** — Structural shell. Three-zone flex row: left sidebar → canvas → right sidebar. Uses Framer Motion for animated entry/exit.
- **`BuilderHeader.tsx`** — Top bar. Project name editing, save status, and actions.
- **`BuilderSidebar.tsx`** — Collapsible side panels (left/right). Wraps `CollapsibleSidePanel`, drives width transitions, has a "Stable Manifest" footer.
- **`BuilderCanvas.tsx`** — Central viewport. Zoom orchestration, scroll area, dot-grid atmosphere, crop marks, floating zoom HUD.
- **`SidebarContainer.tsx`** — Inner panel wrapper. Dot-grid, sticky technical header, scrollable content.
- **`SidebarSection.tsx`** — Collapsible grouping within a panel. Animated height, high-density labels.
- **`types.ts`** — Shared prop interfaces (`SidebarPanelConfig`, `BuilderSidebarProps`).

---

### Refactoring Goals

Please refactor these components to professional engineering standards with the following objectives:

---

#### 1. 🔧 Structural & Responsibility Clarity

- **`BuilderWorkspace.tsx`** is doing too much: fullscreen logic, onboarding state, snapshot lookup, profiler instrumentation, suggestion computation, and layout composition. Extract each concern into a dedicated hook or sub-component:
  - `useFullscreen(ref)` → handles `requestFullscreen`, `exitFullscreen`, and `fullscreenchange` event.
  - `useOnboarding()` → handles `localStorage` check, `showOnboarding` state, and `handleOnboardingComplete`.
  - Move `suggestion` computation into `useReportGenerator` or a dedicated `useDocumentSuggestion(project)` hook.
  - Remove the `<Profiler>` wrapper in production builds (gate it with `process.env.NODE_ENV === 'development'`).

- **`BuilderLayout.tsx`** should accept an optional `leftSidebar` and correctly handle the case where neither sidebar is present (full-width canvas).

- **`BuilderCanvas.tsx`** has two zoom-reset controls (`RotateCcw` and the percentage button) that both call `onZoomReset`. Consolidate into one canonical reset action and clarify intent with distinct `aria-label` values.

---

#### 2. 📐 CSS Variables & Sizing Hygiene

- The CSS variables `--sidebar-w`, `--sidebar-w-left`, and `--workspace-h` are defined inline on the `BuilderLayout` root `div`. Move these into the global CSS (`globals.css`) or a dedicated design-token layer so they are available to child components without prop drilling or `var()` assumptions.
- The `BuilderSidebar` and `BuilderCanvas` currently duplicate the 28px dot-grid background style inline. Extract this into a reusable Tailwind utility class or a shared `<AtmosphericGrid />` primitive component to eliminate duplication across 4+ components.

---

#### 3. 🎬 Motion & Animation Consistency

- `BuilderLayout` uses `mode="popLayout"` for sidebar `AnimatePresence`. Validate that this does not cause layout shifts when the right sidebar transitions between panels. Consider `mode="wait"` if jumps occur.
- All motion transitions use `ease: [0.22, 1, 0.36, 1]` (spring-like cubic bezier). Extract this into a shared constant:
  ```ts
  // src/modules/ai-content/adapters/components/builder/layout/motion.ts
  export const SPRING_EASE = [0.22, 1, 0.36, 1] as const;
  export const PANEL_TRANSITION = { duration: 0.5, ease: SPRING_EASE };
  ```
- `SidebarSection` uses `duration: 0.5` for height animation. Reduce to `0.3` for snappier section toggling which is more standard for collapsible UIs.

---

#### 4. ♿ Accessibility Improvements

- **`SidebarSection`**: The `<button>` already handles `onClick`, so the `onKeyDown` for `Enter` is redundant — native buttons fire `onClick` on Enter. Remove the redundant handler.
- **`SidebarSection`**: Add `aria-expanded={isOpen}` and `aria-controls` pointing to the content `id` for proper screen reader announcement.
- **`BuilderCanvas`** Zoom HUD: The `<button>` for zoom reset percentage is missing `aria-label`. Add `aria-label="Reset zoom to 100%"`.
- **`BuilderSidebar`** footer: The `ShieldCheck` icon and version label are decorative. Ensure they have `aria-hidden="true"`.
- **`SidebarContainer`** header: The `<h2>` is semantically correct, but ensure heading hierarchy is consistent with the page (should be `<h2>` if the page has an `<h1>`, otherwise adjust).

---

#### 5. 🧩 Type Safety & Interface Completeness

- **`BuilderCanvas`**: The `containerRef` prop type is `React.RefObject<HTMLDivElement>` but the component also has its own `ref` via `forwardRef`. The dual-ref pattern is confusing — document when each is used or consolidate.
- **`types.ts`**: `SidebarPanelConfig.icon` is typed as `ReactElement` but is passed directly as JSX. Widen to `ReactNode` for flexibility, or narrow to `React.ReactElement<{ className?: string }>` to allow icon size overrides.
- **`BuilderSidebarProps`**: `defaultSize` and `onResize` are defined but never consumed anywhere in `BuilderSidebar.tsx`. Either implement resizable sidebar logic or remove these dead props.

---

#### 6. 🧹 Code Quality & Naming

- Remove all internal HUD/military jargon from comments (`Neural Matrix`, `Spectral Synchronization`, `Neural Probing Active`, `Registry Node 01`, `Stable Manifest`) and replace with clear, professional engineering terminology:
  - `Neural Matrix` → `Workspace Layout`
  - `Neural Probing Active` → `Processing`
  - `Spectral Overlay` → `Loading Overlay`
  - `Stable Manifest Footer` → `Panel Footer`
  - `Registry Node` → `Panel`
- The hardcoded version label `V2.4.0-S` in `BuilderSidebar`'s footer adds no functional value. Remove it or replace with a dynamic value from `package.json` if needed.
- The `Binary` icon imported in `SidebarContainer.tsx` is unused — remove it.

---

#### 7. 📦 File Organization

- Create `src/modules/ai-content/adapters/components/builder/layout/motion.ts` for shared animation constants.
- Create `src/components/shared/AtmosphericGrid.tsx` for the reusable dot-grid background primitive.
- Ensure `types.ts` is the single source of truth — remove any locally re-declared prop interfaces that shadow it.

---

### Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] `BuilderWorkspace.tsx` is under 100 lines, with logic extracted to hooks.
- [ ] Zero duplicated dot-grid background inline styles — use `<AtmosphericGrid />`.
- [ ] All animation easing constants imported from `motion.ts`.
- [ ] `aria-expanded`, `aria-controls`, and `aria-label` applied to all interactive elements.
- [ ] Dead props (`defaultSize`, `onResize`) either implemented or removed.
- [ ] No internal jargon in JSDoc/comments — professional engineering language only.
- [ ] TypeScript strict mode: no `any`, no unused imports.
- [ ] All components pass existing tests without modification.

---

