2026-04-08 01:08:59.654 | 5617  (5617) | DEBUG    | Processing tool event with attributes: {'gen_ai.tool.name': 'open_files', 'gen_ai.tool.call.id': 'pyd_ai_09a00d31580d428db674f79faa7fa90b', 'tool_arguments': '{"file_paths":["tasks.txt"]}', 'logfire.msg': 'running tool: open_files', 'logfire.json_schema': '{"type": "object", "properties": {"tool_arguments": {"type": "object"}, "tool_response": {"type": "object"}, "gen_ai.tool.name": {}, "gen_ai.tool.call.id": {}}}', 'logfire.span_type': 'span', 'tool_response': '["Successfully opened tasks.txt:\\n\\n````text\\n   0 Now I have a thorough understanding of the entire builder layout system. Here is a professional, detailed refactoring prompt you can use:\\n   1 \\n   2 ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\n   3 \\n   4                                                                       _ Builder Layout Refactoring Prompt\\n   5 \\n   6 ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\n   7                                                                                     Context\\n   8 \\n   9 The Arkan builder workspace is composed of the following layout components located in src/modules/ai-content/adapters/components/builder/layout/:\\n  10 \\n  11  • BuilderWorkspace.tsx — Root orchestrator. Manages fullscreen, onboarding, zoom, and composes all layout pieces.\\n  12  • BuilderLayout.tsx — Structural shell. Three-zone flex row: left sidebar → canvas → right sidebar. Uses Framer Motion for animated entry/exit.\\n  13  • BuilderHeader.tsx — Top bar. Project name editing, save status, and actions.\\n  14  • BuilderSidebar.tsx — Collapsible side panels (left/right). Wraps CollapsibleSidePanel, drives width transitions, has a \\"Stable Manifest\\" footer.\\n  15  • BuilderCanvas.tsx — Central viewport. Zoom orchestration, scroll area, dot-grid atmosphere, crop marks, floating zoom HUD.\\n  16  • SidebarContainer.tsx — Inner panel wrapper. Dot-grid, sticky technical header, scrollable content.\\n  17  • SidebarSection.tsx — Collapsible grouping within a panel. Animated height, high-density labels.\\n  18  • types.ts — Shared prop interfaces (SidebarPanelConfig, BuilderSidebarProps).\\n  19 \\n  20 ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\n  21                                                                                Refactoring Goals\\n  22 \\n  23 Please refactor these components to professional engineering standards with the following objectives:\\n  24 \\n  25 ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\n  26                                                                    1. 🔧 Structural & Responsibility Clarity\\n  27 \\n  28  • BuilderWorkspace.tsx is doing too much: fullscreen logic, onboarding state, snapshot lookup, profiler instrumentation, suggestion computation, and layout composition.\\n  29    Extract each concern into a dedicated hook or sub-component:\\n  30     • useFullscreen(ref) → handles requestFullscreen, exitFullscreen, and fullscreenchange event.\\n  31     • useOnboarding() → handles localStorage check, showOnboarding state, and handleOnboardingComplete.\\n  32     • Move suggestion computation into useReportGenerator or a dedicated useDocumentSuggestion(project) hook.\\n  33     • Remove the <Profiler> wrapper in production builds (gate it with process.env.NODE_ENV === \'development\').\\n  34  • BuilderLayout.tsx should accept an optional leftSidebar and correctly handle the case where neither sidebar is present (full-width canvas).\\n  35  • BuilderCanvas.tsx has two zoom-reset controls (RotateCcw and the percentage button) that both call onZoomReset. Consolidate into one canonical reset action and clarify\\n  36    intent with distinct aria-label values.\\n  37 \\n  38 ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\n  39                                                                      2. 📐 CSS Variables & Sizing Hygiene\\n  40 \\n  41  • The CSS variables --sidebar-w, --sidebar-w-left, and --workspace-h are defined inline on the BuilderLayout root div. Move these into the global CSS (globals.css) or a\\n  42    dedicated design-token layer so they are available to child components without prop drilling or var() assumptions.\\n  43  • The BuilderSidebar and BuilderCanvas currently duplicate the 28px dot-grid background style inline. Extract this into a reusable Tailwind utility class or a shared\\n  44    <AtmosphericGrid /> primitive component to eliminate duplication across 4+ components.\\n  45 \\n  46 ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\n  47                                                                      3. 🎬 Motion & Animation Consistency\\n  48 \\n  49  • BuilderLayout uses mode=\\"popLayout\\" for sidebar AnimatePresence. Validate that this does not cause layout shifts when the right sidebar transitions between panels. Consider\\n  50    mode=\\"wait\\" if jumps occur.\\n  51  • All motion transitions use ease: [0.22, 1, 0.36, 1] (spring-like cubic bezier). Extract this into a shared constant:\\n  52    ```ts\\n  53    // src/modules/ai-content/adapters/components/builder/layout/motion.ts\\n  54    export const SPRING_EASE = [0.22, 1, 0.36, 1] as const;\\n  55    export const PANEL_TRANSITION = { duration: 0.5, ease: SPRING_EASE };\\n  56    ```\\n  57  • SidebarSection uses duration: 0.5 for height animation. Reduce to 0.3 for snappier section toggling which is more standard for collapsible UIs.\\n  58 \\n  59 ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\n  60                                                                        4. ♿ Accessibility Improvements\\n  61 \\n  62  • SidebarSection: The <button> already handles onClick, so the onKeyDown for Enter is redundant — native buttons fire onClick on Enter. Remove the redundant handler.\\n  63  • SidebarSection: Add aria-expanded={isOpen} and aria-controls pointing to the content id for proper screen reader announcement.\\n  64  • BuilderCanvas Zoom HUD: The <button> for zoom reset percentage is missing aria-label. Add aria-label=\\"Reset zoom to 100%\\".\\n  65  • BuilderSidebar footer: The ShieldCheck icon and version label are decorative. Ensure they have aria-hidden=\\"true\\".\\n  66  • SidebarContainer header: The <h2> is semantically correct, but ensure heading hierarchy is consistent with the page (should be <h2> if the page has an <h1>, otherwise\\n  67    adjust).\\n  68 \\n  69 ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\n  70                                                                   5. 🧩 Type Safety & Interface Completeness\\n  71 \\n  72  • BuilderCanvas: The containerRef prop type is React.RefObject<HTMLDivElement> but the component also has its own ref via forwardRef. The dual-ref pattern is confusing —\\n  73    document when each is used or consolidate.\\n  74  • types.ts: SidebarPanelConfig.icon is typed as ReactElement but is passed directly as JSX. Widen to ReactNode for flexibility, or narrow to React.ReactElement<{ className?:\\n  75    string }> to allow icon size overrides.\\n  76  • BuilderSidebarProps: defaultSize and onResize are defined but never consumed anywhere in BuilderSidebar.tsx. Either implement resizable sidebar logic or remove these dead\\n  77    props.\\n  78 \\n  79 ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\n  80                                                                           6. 🧹 Code Quality & Naming\\n  81 \\n  82  • Remove all internal HUD/military jargon from comments (Neural Matrix, Spectral Synchronization, Neural Probing Active, Registry Node 01, Stable Manifest) and replace with\\n  83    clear, professional engineering terminology:\\n  84     • Neural Matrix → Workspace Layout\\n  85     • Neural Probing Active → Processing\\n  86     • Spectral Overlay → Loading Overlay\\n  87     • Stable Manifest Footer → Panel Footer\\n  88     • Registry Node → Panel\\n  89  • The hardcoded version label V2.4.0-S in BuilderSidebar\'s footer adds no functional value. Remove it or replace with a dynamic value from package.json if needed.\\n  90  • The Binary icon imported in SidebarContainer.tsx is unused — remove it.\\n  91 \\n  92 ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\\n  93                                                                             7. 📦 File Organization\\n  94 \\n  95  • Create src/modules/ai-content/adapters/components/builder/layout/motion.ts for shared animation constants.\\n  96  • Create src/components/shared/AtmosphericGrid.tsx for the reusable dot-grid background primitive.\\n  97  • Ensure types.ts is the single source of truth — remove any locally re-declared prop interfaces that shadow it.\\n  98 \\n  99 ────────────────────────────────────────────────