2026-04-08 01:17:21.347 | 5617  (5617) | DEBUG    | Model response text: I have completed the professional refactoring of the builder layout components. The workspace has been transformed from a jargon-heavy implementation into a clean, modular, and accessible engineering environment.

### Key Improvements

#### 🏗️ Architecture & Logic
- **Decoupled `BuilderWorkspace`**: Extracted over 100 lines of logic into three specialized hooks: `useFullscreen`, `useOnboarding`, and `useDocumentSuggestion`.
- **Performance**: Standardized `Profiler` usage to only run in development environments.
- **Shared Infrastructure**: Created `motion.ts` for standardized animation constants and `AtmosphericGrid.tsx` to eliminate redundant inline styles for the background grid.

#### 🎨 Design & Consistency
- **Design Tokens**: Moved hardcoded workspace dimensions (`--sidebar-w`, etc.) into `globals.css` root variables.
- **Professional Terminology**: Replaced all internal jargon ("Neural Matrix", "Spectral Analysis", "Registry Node") with professional engineering terms like "Workspace Layout", "Processing", and "Navigator".
- **Refined UX**: Snappier sidebar transitions (reduced to 0.3s) and consolidated zoom-reset controls.

#### ♿ Accessibility & Quality
- **Screen Reader Support**: Added `aria-expanded`, `aria-controls`, and `useId` to all collapsible sections.
- **Interactive Elements**: Applied descriptive `aria-label` tags to zoom controls and toolbar actions.
- **Type Safety**: Improved `SidebarPanelConfig` interfaces to support flexible icon rendering and removed dead props across the layout suite.

### Summary of Changed Files
- `src/app/globals.css`: Integrated layout tokens.
- `src/components/shared/AtmosphericGrid.tsx`: **New** shared background component.
- `src/modules/ai-content/adapters/components/builder/layout/motion.ts`: **New** animation constants.
- `src/modules/ai-content/adapters/hooks/builder/`: **New** logic hooks (`useFullscreen.ts`, `useOnboarding.ts`, `useDocumentSuggestion.ts`).
- `src/modules/ai-content/adapters/components/builder/BuilderWorkspace.tsx`: Cleaned and modularized.
- `src/modules/ai-content/adapters/components/builder/layout/`: Hardened `BuilderLayout`, `BuilderCanvas`, `BuilderSidebar`, `SidebarSection`, and `SidebarContainer`.
- `src/modules/ai-content/adapters/components/builder/renderer/DocumentRenderer.tsx`: Standardized error boundaries and removed jargon.
- `src/modules/ai-content/adapters/components/builder/layout/types.ts`: Refined type definitions.

The builder is now more robust, maintainable, and aligned with industry-standard professional UI patterns.

What would you like to do next?
1. **Verify the changes** by running the development server?
2. **Review the new hooks** in detail?
3. **Refactor another module** (e.g., the File Manager or AI Generation HUDs) using similar professional standards?
