### Key Refactorings

#### 🛠️ Architecture & Consolidation
- **Merged Components**: Consolidated `DocumentToolbarBase.tsx` into `DocumentToolbar.tsx`. The previous two-file structure was a thin wrapper that added unnecessary complexity. `DocumentToolbar.tsx` is now the single source of truth for the toolbar.
- **Improved Type Safety**: Refined the `DocumentToolbarProps` interface and ensured strict TypeScript compliance throughout the file.

#### 🎨 Design & Terminology
- **Professional Vocabulary**:
    - "Live" → **"Connected"**: Standardized the connection status indicator.
    - "Intelligent Suggestion" → **"Writing Assistant"**: Aligned the AI guidance label with industry-standard professional terminology.
    - "Not saved yet" → **"Draft"**: Simplified the persistence status indicator.
- **Consistent Styling**: Applied the high-density label style (`text-[9px] font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em]`) to the "Connected", "Format", and "Assistant" sections to match the sidebar and header.
- **Motion Integration**: Integrated the `SPRING_EASE` constant for view-mode transitions, ensuring a smooth, premium feel across the workspace.

#### ♿ Accessibility & UX
- **Enhanced Tooltips**: 
    - Added standard keyboard shortcuts (e.g., `Ctrl+B`, `Ctrl+Alt+1`) to all formatting tooltips.
    - Standardized descriptions (e.g., "Preview Document" instead of "Switch to Preview").
- **Interactive Hardening**: Added descriptive `aria-label` tags to all formatting and view-control buttons for better screen reader support.

### Summary of Changes
- `src/modules/ai-content/adapters/components/builder/toolbar/DocumentToolbar.tsx`: **Updated** with consolidated logic, professional labels, and enhanced tooltips.
- `src/modules/ai-content/adapters/components/builder/toolbar/DocumentToolbarBase.tsx`: **Deleted** after merging logic into the primary component.

